\subsection{Ablation Studies}
\label{ablation}
We compare AECS to exhaustive traversal of all possible core selections to demonstrate optimality and efficiency. Besides, we also analyze how our heuristic-averaged energy objective enhances robustness. Results are shown in Table \ref{tab:ablation}.

\textbf{Optimality and Efficiency: compare to exhaustive traversal.} We conduct exhaustive traversal on all test devices and observe that the searched results are exactly the same as AECS results, which means the optimality rate of AECS is 100\%. The search space of exhaustive traversal scales up to 20-71, taking up 10-20 minutes of foreground execution, which is intolerable for users. AECS successfully removes uncompetitive candidates so that the search time is reduced to 1-2 minutes. The results indicate that AECS has the same optimality rate as exhaustive search while being $10\times$ faster.

