    The orange line shows a fit of the measured N$_{123}$ spectrum. One-time scattered electrons are visible as a rate increase approximately 13\,eV below the main peak (purple). Changes of this distance $\Delta_{10}[V]$ are an observable of the inhomogeneity of the electric potential. Changes of the line width of the non-scattered electrons are given by the standard deviation $\sigma_0[V]$ of the potential. The N$_1$ line coincides with the scattering and is a nuisance in these measurements. Plot from~\cite{KryptonMeasurementPaper}.}
    \label{fig:KryptonN123Spectrum}
