%\cite{Kruskal1956}. All these algorithms have runtime either $O(m \log n)$ or $O(m+n\log n)$, where $m$ and $n$ denote the number of edges and nodes of $G$, respectively. Later studies improved runtime to linear \cite{KargerKT95} or very close to it \cite{Chazelle00a}.
