Maximal Independent Set (MST) and Maximal Dominating Set (MDS) problems were also studied recently in the agentic model \cite{PattanayakBCM24,ChandMS23} assuming $k=n$ and parameters $n,\Delta$ (additionally $m$ and $\gamma$, the number of clusters in the initial configuration, for MDS \cite{ChandMS23}) are known to agents a priori. %\manish{Not sure whether we should cite the MDS paper here.} 
Leader election and MST were studied in the agentic model for the case of $k=n$ with known parameters in \cite{KshemkalyaniICDCIT25} and without known parameters in \cite{kshemkalyani2024agent,KshemkalyaniAAMAS25}. The proposed results in this paper are the first for any graph level task, including leader election and MST, in the agentic model for the case of $k<n$. 

