\noindent{\bf Time Cycle.}
%At any time a agent $r_i\in \cR$ could be active or inactive. 
An active agent $r_i$ performs
the ``Communicate-Compute-Move'' (CCM) cycle as follows. (i) {\em Communicate:} Let $r_i$ be on node $v_i$. For each agent $r_j\in \cR$ that is co-located at $v_i$,  $r_i$ can observe the memory of $r_j$, including its own memory; 
%agent~$r_i$ can also observe its own memory. 
(ii) {\em Compute:} $r_i$ may perform an arbitrary computation
using the information observed during the ``communicate'' portion of
that cycle. This includes determination of a (possibly) port to 
use to exit $v_i$, the information to carry while exiting, and the information to store in
%the whiteboard memory at $v_i$ and 
the agent(s) $r_j$ that stays at $v_i$;
(iii) {\em Move:} $r_i$ writes new information (if any) in the memory of an agent $r_j$ at $v_i$,  and exits $v_i$ using the computed port to reach to a neighbor node of $v_i$. 
