Because Omega Cen is an old stellar population, the majority of our TDEs originate from low-mass MS stars, see Figure~\ref{fig:tde_masses}. At $0.5$~Gyr, the typical TDE mass is $0.55 \, \msun$, decreasing to $0.38 \, \msun$ at $12$~Gyr. Additionally, the total number of TDEs decreases with time due to the gradual expansion of the cluster, causing lower densities near the IMBH. 


