which is readily evaluated. In this example, we demonstrate the applicability of the method for the more general initial condition $u_0(z)\in[0,1]$ shown in (cf.~Fig.~\ref{fig:u0_z}). This function is compactly supported on $\mathbb{R}^2$ and we evaluate the integral term $\hat{u}_p$ in \eqref{eq:particularsol} via quadrature. The shown solution profiles $u(z,t)$ display the smoothing effects of the heat equation on the discontinuities in the initial profile. For our geometry, we adopt our configuration in Fig. \ref{fig:sigma} with Runge expansions at $z_{*1}=5+2.5i$ and $z_{*2}=4.5+3i$.

